    fields:  # cee3
      statement: "AnalysisRun.repo_fingerprint should identify the analyzed repository state at the time of the run, enabling cross-run identity ('was this the same repo, was it modified?'). Today it is None on 100% of 133 AnalysisRuns on hypergumbo's own behavior map."  # cee3
      root_cause: "The field is declared in the AnalysisRun dataclass and serialized into every analysis_runs[] entry, but no producer in the analyzer pipeline writes a non-None value. Same dead-field pattern as WI-fanun (Symbol.fingerprint), WI-bujim (features[]), WI-lonoz (Edge.quality) — schema field declared but no code path populates."  # cee3
- op: update  # 2e45
  at: '2026-05-17T21:42:21Z'  # 2e45
  by: agent  # 2e45
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2e45
  clock: 2  # 2e45
  nonce: '2e45'  # 2e45
  set:  # 2e45
    description: "**REVISED 2026-05-17 — original dead-schema-field framing was wrong.** Investigation found that `AnalysisRun.repo_fingerprint` has a fully spec-defined algorithm at `docs/hypergumbo-spec.md:378-384`. The 100% null state is a producer gap, not a vestigial field.\n\n## Empirical observation (unchanged)\n\nOn hypergumbo's self-analysis, `AnalysisRun.repo_fingerprint` is `None` on every one of 133 runs. The field is declared in the `AnalysisRun` dataclass and serialized into every `analysis_runs[]` entry, but no producer in the analyzer pipeline writes a non-None value.\n\n## What the spec actually says\n\nThe field is **fully specified** at `docs/hypergumbo-spec.md:378-384`:\n\n> `repo_fingerprint`: Hash identifying the code snapshot analyzed\n> - Git repos: `sha256(git_head + sorted([(path, sha256(content_bytes)) for each dirty file]))`\n>   - `git_head`: HEAD commit hash\n>   - `dirty file`: tracked file whose working tree content differs from HEAD OR untracked file included in analysis\n>   - Purpose: ensures repo_fingerprint changes when dirty file contents change, not just when paths change\n> - Non-git: `sha256(sorted([(path, content_hash) for all files]))`\n> - Purpose: Cache invalidation, provenance tracking\n\nAlgorithm. Inputs. Both git and non-git branches. Purpose. The spec also declares a top-level `repo_fingerprint_scheme: \"hypergumbo-repofp-v1\"` (line 660) identifying the algorithm version. Schema declares the field at `docs/schema.json:935`.\n\n**The field is not vestigial — the implementation just never caught up to the spec.**\n\n## Cross-reference: connection to INV-magul\n\nThe codebase has a **different** repo-state-hash function at `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/sketch_embeddings.py:1278-1376` — `_get_repo_state_hash()` — used for cache sharding. Comparing it with the spec-defined algorithm:\n\n| Function | Inputs | Used for |\n|---|---|---|\n| Spec lines 378-384 | `git_head` + per-dirty-file `sha256(content_bytes)` | `AnalysisRun.repo_fingerprint` (declared, never populated) |\n| `_get_repo_state_hash()` | `git rev-parse HEAD` + `sha256(git diff HEAD)[:8]` + `sha256(path:size:mtime per untracked)[:8]` | Cache shard key (used in production) |\n\nSimilar but **not identical**. The spec's algorithm uses content-bytes-per-dirty-file (stable across mtime changes); the cache shard uses git-diff-blob + path:size:mtime (sensitive to mtime). The cache shard's mtime sensitivity is exactly what makes `INV-magul` (cache shard polluted by tracker `.ops` churn) misbehave.\n\n**Concrete fix opportunity.** If this item is implemented by extracting a shared `compute_repo_fingerprint(repo_root, dirty_files)` function per the spec algorithm, the cache layer in `sketch_embeddings.py` can optionally migrate to it. The migration would fix `INV-magul`'s tracker-churn pollution as a side effect: content-hashing doesn't pick up mtime jitter the way path:size:mtime does.\n\nThat makes `INV-tofur` and `INV-magul` a coupled pair worth coordinating.\n\n## Severity\n\nMedium. Affects:\n- **Cross-run identity claims**: \"was this the same repo state?\" returns no signal today.\n- **Cache invalidation**: spec line 384 lists \"Cache invalidation, provenance tracking\" as the purpose. The cache layer uses its own hash because the spec-defined one was never built.\n- **Schema consistency**: `repo_fingerprint_scheme` declared at top-level, scheme version \"hypergumbo-repofp-v1\" — but no field actually carrying that scheme's output.\n\n## Fix proposal\n\n1. **Implement the spec-defined algorithm** at lines 378-384 as a shared function (probably in `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/profile.py` or a new `repo_fingerprint.py`). Both branches (git and non-git). Property tests on small fixtures including dirty-file-with-mtime-change-only (must produce same hash) and dirty-file-with-content-change (must produce different hash).\n2. **Populate `AnalysisRun.repo_fingerprint`** at run construction time. ~half day total.\n3. **(Optional but recommended)** Migrate `_get_repo_state_hash()` to call the shared function. This addresses `INV-magul`'s cache pollution as a side effect. Verify cache continuity (existing cache entries become unreachable; either invalidate explicitly or accept the one-time miss).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Self-analysis dogfood: `analysis_runs[*].repo_fingerprint` is non-null on every run.\n- Property test: two runs on the same repo state (same HEAD, same dirty-file contents) produce the same fingerprint.\n- Property test: changing a dirty file's content changes the fingerprint; changing only mtime does NOT.\n- Schema validation passes: top-level `repo_fingerprint_scheme` matches the algorithm used.\n- (If optional step 3 lands) `INV-magul`'s reproducer (run analysis, do a `tracker show`, run analysis again, observe identical shard) passes.\n\n## Related items\n\n- `INV-magul` (P2 violated) — cache shard pollution from tracker `.ops` churn. Loose coupling via the shared-function opportunity (see Cross-reference section above).\n- `WI-fanun` / `INV-sotiv` / `WI-luvig` — write-side identity fields parented under META `INV-zadum`. This item is *not* about Symbol identity; it's about *run* identity. Adjacent concern.\n- `WI-lonoz` (`Edge.quality`) / `WI-bujim` (`features[]`) — companion \"spec promised, impl didn't deliver\" items but different shapes (those are 🟪-or-design-divergence; this one is implementable-as-specified)."  # 2e45
    fields:  # 2e45
      root_cause: "Spec at docs/hypergumbo-spec.md:378-384 fully defines the repo_fingerprint algorithm (git_head + sha256-per-dirty-file for git repos; sha256-of-sorted-(path, content_hash) for non-git). Schema declares the field at docs/schema.json:935. The top-level repo_fingerprint_scheme \"hypergumbo-repofp-v1\" declares the algorithm version. But no producer in the analyzer pipeline computes the spec-defined hash and writes it to AnalysisRun.repo_fingerprint — pure producer gap, not vestigial field. Adjacent function _get_repo_state_hash() in sketch_embeddings.py:1278-1376 uses a SIMILAR-BUT-DIFFERENT algorithm (git diff HEAD blob hash + path:size:mtime for untracked) for cache sharding; that function is the subject of INV-magul (cache shard pollution by tracker .ops file mtime churn). Implementing the spec-defined algorithm as a shared function creates an opportunity to migrate the cache layer and incidentally fix INV-magul."  # 2e45
- op: discuss  # a204
  at: '2026-05-17T21:42:46Z'  # a204
  by: agent  # a204
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a204
  clock: 3  # a204
  nonce: a204  # a204
  message: "Cross-item review 2026-05-17: investigation found this is a producer gap, not a vestigial field. docs/hypergumbo-spec.md:378-384 fully specifies the repo_fingerprint algorithm (git_head + sha256-per-dirty-file for git repos; sha256-of-sorted-(path, content_hash) for non-git), purpose ('Cache invalidation, provenance tracking'), and scheme version ('hypergumbo-repofp-v1' at line 660). Schema declares the field at :935. The field has design intent AND a documented algorithm AND a schema declaration; producers just never implemented it.\n\nImportant cross-reference to INV-magul (cache shard polluted by tracker .ops churn): the adjacent _get_repo_state_hash() at sketch_embeddings.py:1278-1376 uses a similar-but-different algorithm (git diff HEAD blob hash + path:size:mtime for untracked) for cache sharding. The path:size:mtime branch is exactly what makes INV-magul's tracker-.ops mtime jitter pollute the cache. If THIS item is implemented by extracting a shared compute_repo_fingerprint() function per the spec's content-hash algorithm, the cache layer can migrate to it and INV-magul's pollution clears as a side effect (content hashes don't pick up mtime jitter).\n\nDescription rewritten to reflect the spec-defined algorithm, ~half-day implementation scope, and the INV-magul coupling. fields.root_cause updated correspondingly. Original 'dead-schema-field' framing was wrong."  # a204
